module

public import FormalConjecturesUtil

/-!
# Problem 21.150

by V. I. Zenkov

The answer is no. Let $A = \mathbb{F}_3[x, y]/I^3$, where $I = (x, y)$, and let $B$ be the group
of automorphisms of $A$ generated by multiplication by $1 + x$ and $1 + y$. For $G = A \rtimes B$
and $a = 1$, the subgroup $Z(H) \cap H'$ of $H = \langle a, B \rangle$ has rank $3$, while $B$ has
rank $2$ [vDJMM, Theorem 9.1].

The statement below takes $G$ finite, with $A$ and $B$ elementary abelian for the same prime
$p$; the counterexample has this form. The rank of an elementary abelian $p$-group of order $p^r$
is $r$. The subgroup $Z(H) \cap H'$ lies in $A$, since $G / A$ is abelian.

*References:*
- [The Kourovka Notebook](https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v48), Problem 21.150.
- [vDJMM] W. van Doorn, E. Judin, P. Monticone and D. Morrison, *On some problems from the
  Kourovka Notebook*, [arXiv:2607.17477](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.17477).
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Kourovka.«21.150»

/-- The subgroup $A$ is elementary abelian of exponent dividing $p$. -/
def IsElementaryAbelian {G : Type*} [Group G] (p : ℕ) (A : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  (∀ x ∈ A, ∀ y ∈ A, x * y = y * x) ∧ ∀ x ∈ A, x ^ p = 1

/--
Let $G$ be an extension of a normal elementary abelian subgroup $A$ by an elementary abelian
group $B \cong G/A$ such that $A$ contains an element $a$ with $C_B(a) = 1$. Is it true that the
rank of the subgroup $Z(\langle a, B \rangle) \cap \langle a, B \rangle'$ is at most the rank of
$B$?
-/
@[category research solved, question, AMS 20,
  formal_proof using lean4 at
    "https://github.com/pitmonticone/Kourovka/blob/dcfdbdad8c434e30f6151fb3b4343364d70eeed4/Kourovka/Problem_21_150.lean#L468-L477"]
theorem kourovka_21_150 :
    ¬ ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] [Finite G] (p : ℕ), p.Prime →
      ∀ A B : Subgroup G, A.Normal → IsElementaryAbelian p A → IsElementaryAbelian p B →
        A ⊓ B = ⊥ → A ⊔ B = ⊤ →
        ∀ a ∈ A, (∀ b ∈ B, b * a = a * b → b = 1) →
          let H := Subgroup.closure (insert a (B : Set G))
          Nat.log p (Nat.card ↥(Subgroup.centralizer (H : Set G) ⊓ H ⊓ ⁅H, H⁆)) ≤
            Nat.log p (Nat.card B) := by
  sorry

end Kourovka.«21.150»
